course: dictionary
lesson: 15334
title: Snowfall: the snow, and how much of it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Snowfall is a noun, and it has two meanings. First, it is the snow falling from the sky, the time when the snow comes down. «The snowfall began just after lunch.» Second, it is how much snow falls in a place over a certain time. This amount is measured in centimetres or inches.
explain: Look at the words around it to choose the meaning. «The heavy snowfall closed the road to the village.» Heavy tells you there was a lot of snow, and the road closed, so snowfall means the snow itself. «Yesterday's snowfall was 5 centimetres.» Here a number and a measurement show that snowfall means the amount.
explain: Snowfall often appears in phrases like «heavy snowfall», «light snowfall», «annual snowfall» and «a fresh snowfall». Annual means over one whole year. A fresh snowfall is new snow that has just fallen. Use the first word in each phrase to help you understand the second.
fact: Snowfall is a noun, so you can say a snowfall or snowfalls.
fact: Snowfall can mean the snow falling, or the amount of snow that falls.
fact: Snowfall is measured in centimetres or inches.
fact: «Heavy snowfall» means a lot of snow; «light snowfall» means only a little.
fact: Weather reports use snowfall to warn people when roads may be dangerous.
exercise: «The snowfall began just after lunch.» What does snowfall mean here? | A measurement of rain | A map showing the snow on the hills | A sled made for the snow | *Snow falling from the sky
exercise: «Yesterday's snowfall was 5 centimetres.» What is measured in centimetres here? | The snow falling from the sky | The sky | The road | *The amount of snow that fell
exercise: «Monday's snowfall was 6 centimetres. Tuesday's snowfall was 4 centimetres.» How much more snow fell on Monday? | 4 centimetres | 10 centimetres | 6 centimetres | *2 centimetres
test: «The light snowfall covered the grass in a thin layer.» What does light snowfall mean? | *A small amount of snow | A very heavy amount of snow | Snow that falls only at night | A snowball fight
test: Which phrase means the amount of snow that falls in one whole year? | A fresh snowfall | Light snowfall | *Annual snowfall | Heavy snowfall
exam: Which word in «The heavy snowfall closed the road» tells you there was a lot of snow? | road | *heavy | snowfall | closed
